{"code":"19-1012.00","title":"Food Scientists and Technologists","description":"Use chemistry, microbiology, engineering, and other sciences to study the principles underlying the processing and deterioration of foods; analyze food content to determine levels of vitamins, fat, sugar, and protein; discover new food sources; research ways to make processed foods safe, palatable, and healthful; and apply food science knowledge to determine best ways to process, package, preserve, store, and distribute food.","jobZone":4,"kinds":{"R":{"score":5.05,"share":0.2547},"I":{"score":5.71,"share":0.2962},"A":{"score":2.45,"share":0.0912},"S":{"score":2.16,"share":0.073},"E":{"score":2.58,"share":0.0994},"C":{"score":3.95,"share":0.1855}},"highPoints":["I","R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":7494,"text":"Inspect food processing areas to ensure compliance with government regulations and standards for sanitation, safety, quality, and waste management.","core":true,"importance":4.38,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.73},{"id":7486,"text":"Check raw ingredients for maturity or stability for processing, and finished products for safety, quality, and nutritional value.","core":true,"importance":4.18,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.64},{"id":7489,"text":"Study methods to improve aspects of foods, such as chemical composition, flavor, color, texture, nutritional value, and convenience.","core":true,"importance":4.18,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.05},{"id":7492,"text":"Develop food standards and production specifications, safety and sanitary regulations, and waste management and water supply specifications.","core":true,"importance":4.14,"relevance":100,"frequency":2.86},{"id":7487,"text":"Confer with process engineers, plant operators, flavor experts, and packaging and marketing specialists to resolve problems in product development.","core":true,"importance":4,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.95},{"id":7490,"text":"Study the structure and composition of food or the changes foods undergo in storage and proc